      ["A pinch of salt", "Murray River salt for salinity — the thing that makes a sip ask for the next one."],
      ["Verjus pressed", "Unripe Semillon grapes from the Barossa Valley, pressed into verjus. Acidity without vinegar."],
      ["Tasted to level", "Sugar goes in last, only as much as the raspberries need."]
    ]
  },
  {
    code: "NON2", name: "NON2 — CARAMELISED PEAR & KOMBU", accent: "#D57534",
    fruit: "pear", bot: "kelp",
    caps: ["PEARS · CARAMELISED", "BLACK TEA · SPICE", "KOMBU · OLIVE BRINE", "SEMILLON · VERJUS", "AGAVE · VANILLA"],
    steps: [
      ["Caramelised", "Pears cooked until their sugars darken, then steeped. Buttery body, no butter."],
      ["Tea & spice", "Black tea for structure, with clove, cardamom, star anise, ginger and peppercorn riding behind it."],
      ["Sea minerality", "Kombu and olive brine instead of a straight salt hit — savoury, oceanic depth."],
      ["Verjus pressed", "Verjus cuts the caramel so the body stays bright rather than syrupy."],
      ["Tasted to level", "Agave and vanilla land it, tasted back against the spice."]
    ]
  },
  {
    code: "NON3", name: "NON3 — TOASTED CINNAMON & YUZU", accent: "#ECDEAC",
    fruit: "citrus", bot: "quill",
    caps: ["ORANGE · YUZU", "CINNAMON · TOASTED", "SALT", "SEMILLON · VERJUS", "SUGAR TO TASTE"],
    steps: [
      ["Citrus in", "Oranges and yuzu, juiced and zested — the aromatic lift the whole drink is built around."],
      ["Toasted cinnamon", "Cinnamon is toasted before it goes in. Warmth, and a dry savoury edge underneath the fruit."],
      ["A pinch of salt", "Salt holds the citrus down so it reads as a drink, not as juice."],
      ["Verjus pressed", "Verjus sits behind the yuzu — tart, never sharp."],
      ["Tasted to level", "Sugar to level, tasted against how sweet the oranges came in."]
    ]
  },
  {
    code: "NON5", name: "NON5 — LEMON MARMALADE & HIBISCUS", accent: "#E0463E",
    fruit: "citrus", bot: "flower",
    caps: ["LEMON · MARMALADE", "HIBISCUS · LIQUORICE", "SALT · HOPS", "SEMILLON · VERJUS", "SUGAR TO TASTE"],
    steps: [
      ["Cooked down", "Lemon cooked marmalade-style, then layered with lemon verbena, lemongrass and lemon myrtle."],
      ["Hibiscus in", "Hibiscus for colour and grip; liquorice root and peppermint carry the menthol finish."],
